# Adding an app

When the user wants to add an app (URL, author, description, etc.), do this — do **not** build a form or edit HTML cards by hand.

## Steps

1. Open `assets/original_article/db-fixed.json`.
2. Append one object with the next unused `id` (`max(id) + 1`).
3. Fill required fields (see schema below). Infer a short English title/description if the user only gave Polish (or vice versa). Prefer concise catalog blurbs over pasting an entire instruction page unless the user asks to keep the full text.
4. Pick tags only from `TAGS_DESCRIPTORS` in `assets/original_article/generate_site.py`. Typical DIY games: `DIY`, `game`, `learn` (add others only when clearly fitting).
5. Run:
   ```bash
   .venv/bin/python assets/original_article/generate_site.py
   ```
6. Sanity-check: `pytest -q`. Commit only if the user asks.

## Schema (required)

```json
{
  "id": 94,
  "link": "https://example.com/app/",
  "title": { "pl": "", "eng": "App Name" },
  "description": { "pl": "", "eng": "Short blurb." },
  "authors": [{ "name": "Author", "link": "https://…" }],
  "tags": ["DIY", "game"],
  "more_links": []
}
```

- `authors[].link` and `more_links` are optional (`more_links` may be `[]`).
- Omit `created_at` / `last_verified_at` for new apps — the generator sets them.
- Empty `eng` title/description shows as `[TODO TRANSLATE] …` on the site; fill English when you can.
- **Never** hand-edit app cards in `apps.html` — they are regenerated.
- **Never** invent new tags without updating `TAGS_DESCRIPTORS`.

## User paste format (enough)

```
url: …
author: …
author link: …   (optional)
title: …         (optional — infer from site/URL)
description: …
tags: …          (optional — pick sensible defaults)
```
